@API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5095

# Test requests for the Crimson Supply API.
# Sign-in uses a cookie. In VS Code's REST Client the cookie from "Log in"
# is reused automatically for the requests after it.

### ===== Public (no sign-in) =====

### Categories with product counts
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/categories

### Catalog: search, filter and sort (every query parameter is optional)
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products?search=pen&categoryId=1&minPrice=5&maxPrice=20&inStock=true&sort=price-asc

### Best sellers (sort options: featured, popular, newest, price-asc, price-desc, name)
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products?sort=popular&limit=4

### One product
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products/1

### ===== Account =====

### Create a customer account (also signs you in)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "Notebook2026"
}

### Log in
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "Notebook2026"
}

### Who is signed in? (204 = nobody)
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/account/me

### Update my profile
PUT {{API_HostAddress}}/api/account/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "phone": "205-555-0101"
}

### Log out
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/account/logout

### ===== Orders (signed in) =====

### Place an order (prices and totals are calculated by the server)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 7, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### My order history
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/mine

### One order (mine, or any order for an admin)
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/1

### ===== Admin only (sign in as an admin first) =====

### Every order
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/orders

### Change an order's status (Placed, Ready for Pickup, Completed, Cancelled)
PUT {{API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Ready for Pickup" }

### Every product, including hidden ones
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products/manage

### Add a product
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "DSK-399",
  "productName": "Kraft Envelope Pack",
  "description": "Twenty-five 6 x 9 in kraft envelopes.",
  "price": 4.50,
  "stockQuantity": 12,
  "imageUrl": "Resources/Images/products/folders.svg",
  "categoryId": 3
}

### Restock (+) or write off (-) inventory
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "change": 25 }

### Hide a product from the store (true shows it again)
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/products/1/active
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### Add a category
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryName": "Seasonal", "description": "Limited-time items." }

### The five business reports
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/sales-by-product
###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/sales-by-category
###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/sales-by-month
###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/customers
###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/inventory

### Dashboard numbers and the low-stock list
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/summary
###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/reports/low-stock
